Z||000003||Bob Englert||05-25-2001||11:10 PM||||I didn't think any of the 84's had the roller lifters???<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||05-26-2001||12:41 AM||||There's a chance the 84 has roller lifters.  Alot of the 84's had the engines replaced because of the recalls, and the replacement engines had roller lifters.<P>How can you tell what kinda lifters it has from the VIN??||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dwayne Mohr||05-26-2001||07:27 AM||||I haven't opened it up yet to check but according to the parts place if the 8th VIN digit is an R it has rollers.  The stock code according to them would be 2.  You are right I didn't think the used rollers until later. Let you know what I find.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||05-26-2001||07:33 AM||||Hey Dwayne!<BR>If you have a stock 2.5L, it will have the stock lifters, but if it has the roller lifters, they are prone to failure...<BR>Simple job to replace them, but I don't know if the new lifters are any stronger than the old ones...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dwayne Mohr||05-26-2001||07:38 AM|||| Thanks for the info. I can't provide much info about my vehicle. i think i am the third owner and have only had it little over a year.  I was fortunate, it came with both original owners books and inside were a couple of polaroids of it new.  I am going to start on it in a few minutes. Let you kow what I find.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||05-26-2001||05:48 PM||||R VIN simply indicates the cast iron 4 cylinder. There is absolutly nothing in the VIN that tells you what is in the motor.<P>No 84's came stock with rollers. Only an 84 that has had the engine changed Might have them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dwayne Mohr||05-27-2001||12:28 PM||||The Autozone guy was wrong. Just regular hydraulic lifters inside. They were pretty much all clogged.  Replaced the whole set.  The engine runs much quieter now but still have trace of the original noise. I am going to give it a few days and check the torque on the rocker arms. it is kind of a hollow rattle. Goes away above idle. i think it could be a valve too. Any ideas out there?||||reg||1
